{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5b7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a076d5-0351-7d03-9b1f-1385591ddca7"},"sequence":310,"recorded_at":1780531400000615,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"af29e464-8aeb-412a-867f-4ef4384d505f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"af29e464-8aeb-412a-867f-4ef4384d505f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"af29e464-8aeb-412a-867f-4ef4384d505f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"1dc7d6ce-40a4-4303-bd19-4bda0a62f234"},"task_id":"1dc7d6ce-40a4-4303-bd19-4bda0a62f234","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"1dc7d6ce-40a4-4303-bd19-4bda0a62f234","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-17-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board grep \\\"revision.*4\\\" --file \\\"*.json\\\" 2>&1 | head -n 30; echo \\\"===\\\"; task-board grep \\\"base_oid\\\" 2>&1 | head -n 30\",\n  \"description\": \"Find CR revision JSON storage\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"===\\n.resources/BUG-260902-1874eo/BUG-260902-1874eo_review-round3-verdict.md:16:| CR `base_oid` | `8a0dcedf7d1d4a932eae335df2772effe3923cee` |\\n.resources/BUG-260902-3dn8jd/BUG-260902-3dn8jd_rev5-blocker-evidence.md:33:| `initial_base_oid` | `422786cc` | fork point |\\n.resources/BUG-260902-3dn8jd/BUG-260902-3dn8jd_rev5-blocker-evidence.md:35:| `current_base_oid` | `facbd9a8` | refreshed |\\n.resources/BUG-260902-3dn8jd/BUG-260902-3dn8jd_rev5-blocker-evidence.md:36:| `selected_base_oid` | `facbd9a8` | refreshed |\\n.resources/BUG-260902-3dn8jd/BUG-260902-3dn8jd_rev5-blocker-evidence.md:40:`checkpoint_oid == initial_base_oid` means no leaf has ever been checkpointed on\\n.resources/BUG-260902-3dn8jd/BUG-260902-3dn8jd_rev5-blocker-evidence.md:43:`selected_base_oid` followed the authority; `checkpoint_oid` did not. The guard\\n.resources/BUG-260902-3dn8jd/BUG-260902-3dn8jd_rev6-publication-state.md:16:| its `base_oid` | `422786cc` |\\n.resources/BUG-260902-3dn8jd/BUG-260902-3dn8jd_rev6-publication-state.md:19:| workspace `selected_base_oid` | `facbd9a8` |\\n.resources/BUG-260902-3dn8jd/BUG-260902-3dn8jd_rev6-publication-state.md:63:the workspace's `selected_base_oid`; the checkpoint did not follow. Advancing it\\n.resources/BUG-260902-lyhvkw/BUG-260902-lyhvkw_results-recovery-e4f8b2.md:13:fetched at 48db30b (observed 2026-09-02T00:30:42Z); `selected_base_oid`,\\n.resources/BUG-260902-lyhvkw/BUG-260902-lyhvkw_results-recovery-e4f8b2.md:14:`current_base_oid` and `checkpoint_oid` are all 48db30b. The local `main` ref at\\n.resources/TASK-260830-2890sd/TASK-260830-2890sd_review-verdict-rev2.md:14:producer committed before handoff. Here the CR `base_oid` is the **branch tip\\n.resources/TASK-260830-2890sd/TASK-260830-2890sd_review-verdict-rev2.md:18:CR base_oid                       d8fc669af489a58e43ec29ccc3d9d8caedf69f98\\n.resources/TASK-260830-33sfxc/TASK-260830-33sfxc_review-verdict.md:139:`current_base_oid` = `selected_base_oid` = `origin/main` = `d1d3ece`. For a\\n.resources/TASK-260830-33sfxc/TASK-260830-33sfxc_review-verdict.md:147:| Change Request | base_oid | repository_delta |\\n.resources/TASK-260830-34elja/TASK-260830-34elja_review-verdict-rev2.md:12:The CR reports `repository_delta=empty` because its `base_oid` **is** the leaf\\n.resources/TASK-260830-3bkz0c/TASK-260830-3bkz0c_cr-shape-repair-2.md:27:  kind `task_delta`, repository_delta `empty`, base_oid\\n.resources/TASK-260830-3bkz0c/TASK-260830-3bkz0c_cr-shape-repair.md:17:- base_oid: 82c38378fe79b3e2a3e9fa337c23643b856ba7ee (= the delivered commit; zero-byte self-diff)\\n.resources/TASK-260830-3bkz0c/TASK-260830-3bkz0c_review-verdict-rev4.md:20:| rev4 `base_oid` | `82c3837` |\\n.resources/TASK-260830-uqnwmi/TASK-260830-uqnwmi_base-authority-blocker.md:18:| `initial_base_oid` / `current_base_oid` | `48db30b59e5e` (fork point) |\\n.resources/TASK-260830-uqnwmi/TASK-260830-uqnwmi_base-authority-blocker.md:21:| `upstream_oid` / `selected_base_oid` | `10aaa161fafc` |\\nEPIC-260830-37rgqn_m0-contract-foundation/STORY-260830-2jylym_structured-errors-cli-envelope-and-exit-codes/TASK-260830-33sfxc_test-error-and-result-compatibility/progress.md:205:CORRECTION to the orchestrator observation above: the CR base d1d3ece is NOT a stale checkpoint. Workspace WS-4fa8daeca025 has checkpoint_oid correctly reconciled to f34d91d; the CR was built from current_base_oid = origin/main = d1d3ece, which is the right base for a story_final CR whose acceptance is the Story integration unit. The 66-path delta is the whole Story vs trunk and is correct.\\nEPIC-260830-37rgqn_m0-contract-foundation/STORY-260830-2jylym_structured-errors-cli-envelope-and-exit-codes/TASK-260830-34elja_implement-structured-error-registry/progress.md:194:STALE CHANGE-REQUEST WINDOW — READ BEFORE REVIEWING. task-board handoff exited 0 but built NO new CR revision. CR-TASK-260830-34elja-1 is still rev1 with base_oid 4c9efc09bded14e5dcdf96ae0191fb2c15e57cf7 and candidate_tree_oid 42868f86e9823b46b5b390efe1a5e60c0cca2f2f, and its attached patch is empty (sha256 e3b0c442... = zero bytes). That base commit was amended away by this rework and is no longer on the branch; it survives only in the object database.\\nEPIC-260830-37rgqn_m0-contract-foundation/STORY-260830-2jylym_structured-errors-cli-envelope-and-exit-codes/TASK-260830-34elja_implement-structured-error-registry/progress.md:238:ON repository_delta=empty — ACCEPTING AN EMPTY DELTA IS NOT ACCEPTING AN EMPTY DELIVERY. The CR base_oid IS the leaf commit and candidate_tree_oid 49e6cb0d equals both that commit tree and HEAD tree, so the window is zero-width over already-committed work. The delivery is the commit: git diff d1d3ece..ebc4e319 is 20 files +3950/-37, the rework alone 10 files +317/-33. Both reviewed as the real change. Signature verified Good for oparin@me.com, worktree clean, one commit past checkpoint d1d3ece. No repository change would have been the wrong outcome for this leaf and none was made — the code is there and the CR machinery failed to snapshot it twice, for two different reasons (rev1 checkpoint move, rev2 handoff-after-amend). Orchestration defect, not a producer defect, and the producer disclosed it.\\nEPIC-260830-37rgqn_m0-contract-foundation/STORY-260830-3drr2m_session-adapter-and-directory-node-framework/TASK-260830-3bkz0c_prove-shared-environment-implementation-boundary/progress.md:101:Review rev4 (RUN-260906-1c6cfb): ACCEPTED. G-A closed — 7/7 round-1 shapes now fire (was 2/7); 471452 differential vectors (200k random seed 20260907 + 271452 directed) across five judges yield 0 divergence classes, with the instrument validated by a control plant restoring pre-fix dirnode/decode.go that reproduces the round-1 admit witness AND a second over-strict class. G-B closed — battery re-run independently from a fresh baseline: 27 applied, 27 killed, 0 NOT-APPLIED, genuinely narrowing bodies, tree OID unchanged. CORRECTIONS superseding round2.md: (1) refusal-exit denominator is 100 (31 refuse + 58 bool-false + 11 DecodeStrictObject &Fault{} exits), not 89; exit coverage 27 of 100 (27.0%), residue 73; five of the battery mutants target exits the reported denominator excluded. (2) Of the six F1 symbols only DecodeStrictObject gained a production caller; CheckUint53Bounds, CheckSortedUniqueStrings, rawUint53, parseUint53Literal and Fault.Error() remain production-unreachable — 5 of 27 mutants weaken code no product path reaches; boundary.md rows 4-5 name canonical owners, not call sites. (3) Three new census stated bounds, each planted and confirmed green: alias-imported encoding/json strict decoder, byte measure returning (int,error), and any copy outside the seven-entry censusPackages list. (4) rev4 patch is a zero-byte self-diff (base_oid = delivered commit); reviewable delta is 1296ecc..82c3837 inside 1cb6b93..82c3837. Landing: origin/main still 1cb6b93, 4 ahead 0 behind, all commits signature-verified, 19 packages green, go vet + GOOS=windows/linux vet + gofmt + build all clean. Story landable on merit.\\nEPIC-260830-37rgqn_m0-contract-foundation/STORY-260830-3jqsx1_provider-plugin-host-and-protocol/TASK-260830-2890sd_implement-provider-discovery-and-trust/progress.md:207:Round-2 review (RUN-260904-067bc2) at d8fc669: CHANGES REQUESTED -> to-dev. CR rev2 repository_delta=empty is a snapshot artifact: base_oid == branch tip, candidate_tree == HEAD^{tree}, so the CR is NOT stale but carries no window. Real reviewable delta is 292fc6d..d8fc669 (4 files, +286/-3). All five round-1 findings (F1-F5) confirmed FIXED by re-injecting each round-1 mutant at this head. 32 mutants run, 30 caught, 2 survived. F6: injecting an implied-superuser exception into OwnerPolicy.Approves (uid 0 always approved) leaves go test ./... green across all 14 packages -- no test in the package uses uid 0, while provider.go:139, the outcome artifact, and the verbatim-pinned SS7.1 MUST all claim no superuser exception. Isolation probe PASSes intact / FAILs mutated. F7: narrowing the plugin_dirs absolute-path gate to index==0 survives the full suite (delete-only M32 is caught); same shape as F2, whose PATH twin WAS bounded across positions this round. Lower severity -- internal/config validateProviders already rejects non-absolute plugin_dirs. F8: the rev1 verdict supplied a logbook entry to land verbatim; LOGBOOK.md is untouched in 292fc6d..d8fc669 and its newest entry is still 0115. No production behaviour change required. Evidence: TASK-260830-2890sd_review-verdict-rev2.md, TASK-260830-2890sd_review-mutation-log-rev2.md. Also refresh TASK-260830-2890sd_outcome.md -- it still names 292fc6d / 34 PASS / 93.4% (head is d8fc669 / 38 PASS / 94.1%). Worktree left clean at d8fc669; nothing in the repository changed during review.\\nEPIC-260830-37rgqn_m0-contract-foundation/STORY-260830-jeaivu_configuration-loading-and-compatibility/TASK-260830-1qf777_test-config-migration-and-downgrade/progress.md:187:ONE THING FOR THE REVIEWER TO CHECK DEL